    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based membership level 4 in `formatMembershipLevel` in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`.\n\n**Change:** Previously the method computed `level` from the base factors (start at 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) and hard-capped it at 3 with `Math.min(level, 3)`, with level 4 only mentioned as \"reserved for tenure\" but never actually reachable.\n\nNow:\n- The pre-tenure factors are still capped at 3 (`level = Math.min(level, 3)`).\n- A final `+1` is granted only when the owner's tenure \u2014 `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now())` \u2014 is **more than 365 days**.\n\nThis means level 4 requires tenure over 365 days. A newly created owner has `registrationDate` set to today (business day), so tenure is 0 and it can never exceed level 3 \u2014 a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount == 0` lands at exactly level 3, satisfying the `AcceptanceTest` (`membershipLevel` == 3) and all existing tests.\n\nI also updated the method's Javadoc to document the 1\u20134 range and the tenure rule. A null `registrationDate` is handled safely (no tenure bump).",
